# crm-demo scope 100 — look the visitor up in the CRM.
#
# `outlet://crm/query` runs the statement written HERE, in a READ ONLY
# transaction on a pool the chassis owns, with every value bound as a
# parameter ($1 comes from `args`). The op never sees the DSN. The result
# lands at `into`: {ok, outlet, columns, rows: [{col: val}...], count} —
# or {ok: false, error: {code, message}} when anything goes wrong, so the
# next scope branches on `._crm.ok`.
#
# Query params arrive as arrays (?email=a@b → @web.req.url.query.email.0).
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.query.email.0 != ""
  EXEC "outlet://crm/query"
    WITH sql = "SELECT id, name, plan FROM customers WHERE email = $1 LIMIT 10",
         args = &array(@web.req.url.query.email.0),
         into = "_crm"
